# How a backtrace record holds frames for heap profiling

The record is `prof_bt_t` (`include/jemalloc/internal/prof.h:118`):

```c
struct prof_bt_s {
	/* Backtrace, stored as len program counters. */
	void   **vec;
	unsigned len;
};
```

It is only a view: `vec` points at an array of `void *` program counters and `len` says how many are filled in. The struct owns no frame storage itself.

